      "conf": "VERIFIED · PRIMARY AND VENDOR",
      "dek": "US stock futures point higher: the S&P 500 future sits at 7,795.75, up 0.37%, better than the 0.29% of two hours ago. Europe has gone the other way. Germany's DAX is up 0.74% having been up 0.89%, and the FTSE 100 up 0.29% from 0.52%. The reason for the good mood is the same as this morning's, working harder: US oil has fallen to $92.46, down 2.27%, while America and Iran talk about reopening Gulf shipping. Cheaper fuel lifts what companies earn without them selling anything more. Borrowing has not got cheaper, though: the US government still pays 5.18% to borrow for ten years. Watch today's US factory orders at 13:30 UK.",
