      "conf": "VERIFIED · LIVE FEED",
      "dek": "The VIX, Wall Street's fear gauge, measures how much investors are paying to insure their shares. It has fallen to 15.09, down 0.58 on the day, or 3.70%, and that is the lowest it has been today. Thursday's close was 15.67. On the BuyTrigger ladder, 15 to 20 is the normal band: this sits just 0.09 above the calm line and 14.91 below 30, the level at which the system's buy window opens. In plain terms, almost nobody is paying for protection this morning. What to watch is whether today's US factory orders at 13:30 UK disturbs that.",
