      "conf": "CORROBORATED · ONE CLAIM SINGLE SOURCE",
      "dek": "American oil now sells for $12.59 a barrel less than the global Brent price: $92.30 against $104.888, both quoted at the same moment. The gap matters because it says the fall in the oil price is a US story, not a worldwide one. Barrels are being kept at home while Gulf shipping risk still props up the global price. One outlet gave the same gap as $12.68 early this morning, and a second, independent source now confirms it. One caution worth stating plainly: a widely used Brent quote shows $98.30, but that is a November contract, $6.59 below the front month. Watch whether Brent follows US oil down next week.",
